        "original_id": "772c4e9c-c40e-5c6b-8ab9-97a13a7c4ae5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Gerstein, Rudolf Höss\n- Organizations: Waffen-SS, SS, Degesch\n- Places: Auschwitz\n- Roles: Obersturmführer, Head of Technical Disinfection Services, Obersturmbannführer, commandant\n- Products: Zyklon B\n- Documents: Gerstein Report\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Kurt Gerstein wrote the Gerstein Report in 1945.\n- Kurt Gerstein was an Obersturmführer, or first lieutenant, in the Waffen-SS.\n- Kurt Gerstein became the Head of Technical Disinfection Services of the SS.\n- In that SS role, Kurt Gerstein supplied hydrogen cyanide, known as Zyklon B, from Degesch to Rudolf Höss at Auschwitz.\n- In that SS role, Kurt Gerstein conducted negotiations with the owners of Degesch.\n- Rudolf Höss was born on 25 November 1901 and died on 16 April 1947.\n- Rudolf Höss was a Nazi German SS-Obersturmbannführer, or lieutenant colonel.\n- During World War II, Rudolf Höss was the longest-serving commandant of Auschwitz concentration and extermination camp.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e5a262be-c3e0-5c59-9815-fbe3b12b552e",
        "text": "Page: Gerstein Report. Sentence: The Gerstein Report was written in 1945 by Kurt Gerstein, an Obersturmführer (First Lieutenant) of the Waffen-SS who rose to become the Head of Technical Disinfection Services of the SS, and in that capacity supplied hydrogen cyanide (Zyklon B) from Degesch (\"Deutsche Gesellschaft für Schädlingsbekämpfung\") to Rudolf Höss in Auschwitz and conducted the negotiations with the owners.\nPage: Rudolf Höss. Sentence: Rudolf Höss (also Höß, Hoeß or Hoess; 25 November 1901 – 16 April 1947) was a Nazi German \"SS\"-\"Obersturmbannführer\" (lieutenant colonel) and the longest-serving commandant of Auschwitz concentration and extermination camp in World War II.",
